%I A088389 #20 Oct 27 2026 00:12:01
%S A088389 1,1,3,29,940,104286,40050850,53640013886,251995529844792
%N A088389 Number of real regular n X n {0,1}-matrices modulo rows permutations.
%C A088389 To count the number of invertible n X n matrices with entries in any given finite set, we can assume the rows in strictly increasing lexicographical order, and multiply by n! to account for all possible permutations. - _M. F. Hasler_, Oct 26 2026
%H A088389 Antony Pearson, <a href="https://search.proquest.com/openview/1c73b5136e9332a81f1546f910d0e76b">On Hidden Structures in Contaminated Symbolic Data</a>, Ph. D. thesis, University of Colorado at Boulder (2020) 27835343.
%F A088389 a(n) = A055165(n) / n!.
%o A088389 (PARI) apply( {A088389(n, m=2^n-1, A=Mat(), f(x)=Col(binary(x),-n))=if(n, my(r=#A=matconcat([A, Col(0,n)])); sum(b=2^n--, m, A[,r]=f(b); if(matrank(A)==r, A088389(n, b-1, A, f))), 1)}, [0..5]) \\ Only 0.3s up to n=5, but several (> 6) minutes for n=6. - _M. F. Hasler_, Oct 26 2026
%Y A088389 Cf. A055165, A053601.
%K A088389 nonn,hard,more,changed
%O A088389 0,3
%A A088389 Yuval Dekel (dekelyuval(AT)hotmail.com), Nov 08 2003
%E A088389 a(8) from Herman Jamke (hermanjamke(AT)fastmail.fm), Feb 24 2008
